        "original_id": "0b75aff9-0b32-5621-bbcd-28d2718edbf1",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Maria Callas, Vincenzo Bellini\n- Roles: opera singer, opera composer\n- Concepts: opera seria, bel canto\n- Topics: opera repertoire, Italian opera\n\nFacts:\n- Vincenzo Bellini was born on 3 November 1801 and died on 23 September 1835.\n- Vincenzo Bellini’s full name was Vincenzo Salvatore Carmelo Francesco Bellini.\n- Vincenzo Bellini was an Italian opera composer known for long-flowing melodic lines and was called \"the Swan of Catania.\"\n- In her early career, Maria Callas performed the music dramas of Wagner.\n- Maria Callas’s repertoire ranged from classical opera seria to the bel canto operas of Donizetti, Bellini, and Rossini, and also included works by Verdi and Puccini.",
